<title>NETHERLANDS: Major Dutch takeovers in 1996.</title>
<headline>Major Dutch takeovers in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch insurer Aegon's $3.5 billion takeover of U.S. firm Providian Corp's insurance activities is the latest and biggest in a string of big Dutch buys this year.</p>
<p>Following is a list of other key Dutch takeovers in 1996 in order of size:</p>
<p>Nov 22 - ABN AMRO buys Standard Federal Bancorp of the United States for $1.95 billion.</p>
<p>Mar 28 - Retailer Ahold buys Stop &amp; Shop of the U.S. for $1.8 billion.</p>
<p>Oct 1 - Dutch PTT agrees 2.7 billion guilder ($1.6 billion) takeover of Australia's TNT.</p>
<p>Dec 20 - Dutch/Belgian financial services group Fortis buys MeesPierson merchant bank from ABN AMRO for 2.5 billion guilders ($1.43 billion).</p>
<p>Feb 26 - Photocopier maker Oce van der Grinten pays 900 million guilders ($552 million) for the printing arm of Germany's Siemens Nixdorf.</p>
<p>Feb 14 - Home products giant Unilever bids 1.23 billion guilders for Helene Curtis Industries Inc of the U.S.</p>
<p>Nov 4 - Food retailer Ahold buys 50 percent of Brazilian supermarket chain Bompreco which has annual sales of $1.4 billion.</p>
<p>June 3 - Transport group Pakhoed buys U.S. chemical transport firm Univar for $300 million.</p>
<p>Sept 9 - Nedlloyd and P&amp;O merge container businesses, creating $4.0 billion turnover group.</p>
<p>Oct 8 - VNU snaps up near 15 percent stake in Britain's Blenheim, but later loses out in bid race to United News and Media which offered over 590 million stg for Blenheim.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
